config-connector-extensions patch 0063: a regional security policy's rules.

mockgcp's regionSecurityPolicies served insert, get, patch, delete and
list, but not addRule, getRule, patchRule or removeRule, which
ComputeRegionSecurityPolicyRule (ours; foundation item 27) calls. They
are served here (regionsecuritypolicyrules.go): a rule is addressed by its
priority, patchRule replaces the fields its update mask names (a field
unset in the body is cleared) and merges without one, and a missing rule
is 404 (assumed; live pending). A CLOUD_ARMOR policy is made with the
default rule the API adds (allow, priority 2147483647), which removeRule
refuses. The regional patch also takes ddosProtectionConfig and
userDefinedFields, which ComputeRegionSecurityPolicy changes, now that
mockgcp serves that kind's collection. Upstream candidate: yes.

